      "id": 24,
      "title": "Interpretation guardrails",
      "description": "Operator contract for this overview.",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Interpretation guardrails\n- Native panels use supported non-fallback receipt totals with bounded backend and forward-path labels.\n- Gateway TTFT, TPOT, output rate, and prompt-cache ratio are explicitly all-engine context because those emitters have no engine label.\n- Signal-support gauges say whether a measurement is authoritative; they do not substitute a measured zero.\n- Device utilization, memory pressure, queue depth, graph state, and artifact locators are not inferred from receipt data."
      },
      "transparent": true
